# Preparation only. A server administrator must review this for the np2 virtual host.
# Do not add these directives to shared/global Apache or the old WordPress virtual host.
# Requires mod_remoteip and a NONEMPTY, administrator-maintained list of the current
# Cloudflare IPv4/IPv6 networks from https://www.cloudflare.com/ips/ .
# Never enable RemoteIPHeader without the trusted proxy list.
RemoteIPTrustedProxyList /etc/apache2/newspoint-cloudflare-proxies.txt
RemoteIPHeader CF-Connecting-IP

# Keep the application listeners bound to 127.0.0.1:3100 and :3101.
# Restrict external origin access to Cloudflare networks/authorized administrators.
# Cloudflare SSL/TLS mode: Full (strict), valid origin certificate for WEB_URL host.
# The generated .htaccess checks Apache TLS, not untrusted forwarded headers.
